    "comments": {
      "bugs": {
        "2041371": {
          "comments": [
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "aryx.bugmail@gmx-topmail.de",
              "bug_id": 2041371,
              "count": 0,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-21T15:35:48Z",
              "creator": "aryx.bugmail@gmx-topmail.de",
              "id": 18096293,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "Firefox 151.0 and 153.0a1 on Windows 11\n\nIf one copies formatted text (e.g. the summary of this bug) and tries to paste into a document at docs.google.com without formatting by pressing Ctrl+Shift+V, a menu with the single item 'Paste' will be shown (see bug 2021248).\n\nThe position of the menu depends on the mouse cursor:\n* If mouse on same screen as Google doc: menu shown at mouse cursor position\n* If mouse on different screen as Google doc: shown shown at edge of screen with Google doc.\n\nExpected: Menu triggered at caret position where clipboard content shall be inserted.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "Firefox 151.0 and 153.0a1 on Windows 11\n\nIf one copies formatted text (e.g. the summary of this bug) and tries to paste into a document at docs.google.com without formatting by pressing Ctrl+Shift+V, a menu with the single item 'Paste' will be shown (see bug 2021248).\n\nThe position of the menu depends on the mouse cursor:\n* If mouse on same screen as Google doc: menu shown at mouse cursor position\n* If mouse on different screen as Google doc: shown shown at edge of screen with Google doc.\n\nExpected: Menu triggered at caret position where clipboard content shall be inserted.",
              "time": "2026-05-21T15:35:48Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "emilio@crisal.io",
              "bug_id": 2041371,
              "count": 1,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-21T16:03:16Z",
              "creator": "emilio@crisal.io",
              "id": 18096326,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "I think this is a recent regression, maybe a Google Docs change?\n\nI thought that we wouldn't require the popup for pastes with user interaction. Ctrl + V works just fine.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "I think this is a recent regression, maybe a Google Docs change?\n\nI thought that we wouldn't require the popup for pastes with user interaction. Ctrl + V works just fine.",
              "time": "2026-05-21T16:03:16Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "echen@mozilla.com",
              "bug_id": 2041371,
              "count": 2,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-22T09:46:49Z",
              "creator": "echen@mozilla.com",
              "id": 18098194,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "(In reply to Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez [:emilio] from comment #1)\n> I think this is a recent regression, maybe a Google Docs change?\n> \n> I thought that we wouldn't require the popup for pastes with user interaction. Ctrl + V works just fine.\n\nWe only suppress the paste popup when the programmatic clipboard read is issued from a `paste` event handler.\nIn the Google Docs case, it issues `execCommand(\"paste\")` from a `keydown` event handler, where current we don't do special handing for that.\n\nI think we should either show popup in the proper position\nOr\nPerhaps we could optimize for the case where a `keydown` event triggers a paste command. `WidgetKeyboardEvent` might contain the relevant information we need in https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/1f7030c8de8f2b349c7d91d7b5a3253c109a1cc1/widget/TextEvents.h#873-879.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "(In reply to Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez [:emilio] from comment #1)\n> I think this is a recent regression, maybe a Google Docs change?\n> \n> I thought that we wouldn't require the popup for pastes with user interaction. Ctrl + V works just fine.\n\nWe only suppress the paste popup when the programmatic clipboard read is issued from a `paste` event handler.\nIn the Google Docs case, it issues `execCommand(\"paste\")` from a `keydown` event handler, where current we don't do special handing for that.\n\nI think we should either show popup in the proper position\nOr\nPerhaps we could optimize for the case where a `keydown` event triggers a paste command. `WidgetKeyboardEvent` might contain the relevant information we need in https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/1f7030c8de8f2b349c7d91d7b5a3253c109a1cc1/widget/TextEvents.h#873-879.",
              "time": "2026-05-22T09:46:49Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "aryx.bugmail@gmx-topmail.de",
              "bug_id": 2041371,
              "count": 3,
              "creation_time": "2026-05-22T22:52:34Z",
              "creator": "aryx.bugmail@gmx-topmail.de",
              "id": 18099630,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "Yes, a change on the Google Docs side must also be involved. There is a workflow from one month ago with was not affected, this might have regressed in the last 1-3 weeks.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "Yes, a change on the Google Docs side must also be involved. There is a workflow from one month ago with was not affected, this might have regressed in the last 1-3 weeks.",
              "time": "2026-05-22T22:52:34Z"
            },
            {
